    <briefdescription>
<para>Particle-based hydraulic erosion with flow-field coupling (McDonald&apos;s model): persistent per-cell discharge and momentum fields, exponentially filtered across iterations, couple particles through the mean local flow, producing coherent drainage networks; a bank-stability debris flow runs in the same solver loop against a separate sediment layer. Clean-room port of erosiv/soillib (LGPL-3, Nicholas McDonald), <ulink url="https://github.com/erosiv/soillib">https://github.com/erosiv/soillib</ulink>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Parameters are physical: the terrain is interpreted as a world_extent_km x world_extent_km domain with height range z_scale_km. This makes behavior consistent across resolutions.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>Single-resolution runs numerically diverge at high resolutions (&gt;= 1024^2) beyond a few hundred steps with default parameters — use hydraulic_mcdonald_multiscale for high-resolution terrain.</para>
</simplesect>
Results are reproducible up to atomic scheduling order (particles read fields that other particles concurrently modify via atomic adds — a property shared with the reference implementation).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>z</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input/output heightmap. In: bedrock. Out: bedrock plus sediment (total surface). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>steps</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of erosion iterations. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>seed</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Random seed number. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>p_sediment_map</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional output: final sediment layer. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>p_discharge_map</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional output: water discharge field (usable as a river / water mask). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>world_extent_km</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Physical domain edge length [km]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>z_scale_km</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Physical height range of z&apos;s [0, 1] span [km]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>samples</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Particles per iteration. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>maxage</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Maximum particle age (steps along a trajectory). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>lrate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Exponential filter rate for the flow fields. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>time_step</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Geological timestep [y]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rainfall</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Rainfall rate [m/y]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>evap_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Evaporation rate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>gravity</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Gravity [m/s^2]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>viscosity</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Kinematic viscosity (flow-coupling strength). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>bed_shear</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bed shear coefficient. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>crit_slope</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Critical (stable bank) slope [m/m]. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>settle_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Debris settling rate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>thermal_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Thermal erosion rate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>deposition_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Fluvial deposition rate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>suspension_rate</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Fluvial suspension rate. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>exit_slope</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Boundary exit slope [m/m].</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
